      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T20:33:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`SkRect::roundOut()` returns an SkIRect that is basically this calculation, although maybe more correct. As is think there\u0027s a subtle issue with how it rounds out. Ex, we have left \u003d 10.5 and width \u003d 10. The original float rect is spanning 10.5 to 20.5 so typically rounding out would span 10 to 21 (final width \u003d 11). With this code we ceil(10) instead and the final span is 10 to 20.\n\nThis could be part of the flickering that you were seeing when animating float transforms. The other possible cause is that right now ClipStack will represent \"originally\" integer clip rects as just a scissor. With a fractional replay translation, that clip rect should adjust accordingly but would end up popping to integer coordinates. See [1] but I think when the ClipStack is for the replay target, we want to skip this early-out and also mark the corresponding clip elements as used by a draw so that we still record depth-only draws for the clip shapes. These would then respond to the fractional offsets of the replay transform automatically and clip any MSAA samples that are outside the original shape but became visible from rounding out of the integer scissor rect.\n\nWe might also need to update the logic in `CoverBoundsRenderStep` to make sure it always covers the final scissor. Intersection clips use inverse fills to set the depth buffer out to the edge of the scissor rect, but right now [2] draws out to the original scissor coordinates w/o taking into account any rounding. While it would still be translated fractionally, a gap from rounding could lead to MSAA samples at the edge of the replay scissor not actually clipped out. I *think* we just have to pad those draw bounds by 1 to be safe.\n [1]https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/gpu/graphite/ClipStack.cpp;drc\u003deb345886902a18428ba8ccca1033ce7283762483;l\u003d1151\n [2]https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/gpu/graphite/render/CoverBoundsRenderStep.cpp;drc\u003dbd4afe81bde34ce44866a5181eb20c635277931a;l\u003d74",
